# Build context exclusion for `docker compose build`.
#
# Every DIDA Dockerfile builds with the repo root as its context, so without this
# file Docker streams the whole checkout — 1.9 GB of it, most of it _backups —
# into each of forty-odd image builds that COPY a single subdirectory.
#
# node_modules is not merely waste, it is WRONG. Both Node images install from a
# committed lockfile and then copy their source tree over it:
#
#     COPY services/matter-bridge/package.json …/package-lock.json ./
#     RUN npm ci --no-audit --no-fund
#     COPY services/matter-bridge/ ./          <- brings the dev box's node_modules
#
# so the dependency tree `npm ci` just resolved gets overlaid with whatever
# happens to be installed here. That is exactly what those Dockerfiles' own
# comments say they are preventing ("two builds of the same commit could ship
# different bridge code"); the lockfile only actually decides once the host's
# node_modules stops travelling with the source.

# Database dumps and pre-upgrade archives — the biggest thing in the tree and
# nothing builds from them.
_backups/

# Runtime state (postgres data dir, NATS jetstream, clickhouse data) — root-owned
# bind mounts; a rootless builder cannot even read them.
state/
media/
logs/

# Installed dependency trees: every image installs its own from a lockfile.
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
.uv-cache/

# Build outputs and caches that regenerate inside the image.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.svelte-kit/
ui/build/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/

# Signed APKs reach a host as a deploy artifact and are bind-mounted at runtime
# (docker-compose.yml maps ./android/dist to /apk); no image contains them.
android/dist/
android/keystore/

# Repository and editor metadata.
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Secrets never belong in a build context, whatever a Dockerfile asks for.
.env
.env.local
*.secret
.demo-pass
.cf-token

# Test fixtures and demo captures — nothing COPYs them.
tests/
demo-snapshots/

# Coverage runs leave a .cov-<pid> directory behind per process.
.cov-*/
.coverage
htmlcov/
